    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Taylor Ward** (70.00) represent our elite-tier offensive anchors. **Bryson Stott** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Sugano, where a 4.73 xERA and significant platoon advantages push his efficiency score well above the baseline. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** is a high-upside play against Severino; the combination of a high-ceiling park factor (+16%) and a weak SP matchup allows him to maximize his scoring potential despite being slotted lower in the order than preferred. **Brendan Donovan** (65.57) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (62.87) round out the top of our lineup, with **Brendan Donovan** gaining substantial utility from his leadoff spot and a strong platoon edge against Martin.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was keeping **Matt Chapman** (50.16) out of the starting nine. He narrowly missed the cut behind **Geraldo Perdomo** (54.66) and **Masyn Winn** (59.99), with his value slightly capped by a tougher matchup against Chandler and a less favorable spot in the batting order. We are maintaining a disciplined approach to our game caps, ensuring that players like **Matt Chapman** and **Gavin Sheets** remain ready for higher-leverage opportunities. While **Masyn Winn** is starting, it is worth monitoring his matchup against Buehler; despite a high SP xERA, his ability to exploit the pitcher's slow delivery for potential stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014provides a necessary floor that keeps him in the lineup over bench options like **Tyler Freeman**.\n\nAs we monitor the board, we must remain cognizant of the risk inherent in **Jung Hoo Lee** (54.26) facing Chandler. While his leadoff position provides a boost, he faces a significant hurdle in the form of an elite catcher\u2019s arm (1.89s pop time), which effectively nullifies his speed-based value for today\u2019s contest. We are closely tracking official lineup confirmations for **Lawrence Butler** and **Cal Raleigh** to ensure no late-hour shifts disrupt our calculated platoon advantages. Outside of these concerns, the roster is well-positioned to capitalize on these specific pitching matchups.",
